@startuml harness-functions
title Harness functions — framework user, orchestrator agent, step subagents, host, harness

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30
skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Framework user" as User
participant "Workflow Orchestrator agent" as Orch
participant "Step subagent" as Sub
participant "Host\n(e.g. GitHub Copilot)" as Host
participant "Harness" as Harness

note over Harness
  Every completed function invocation appends one
  entry to its session's log — logs/<sessionId>.log.jsonl
  (functions 11-12 run under human or system sessions;
  a workflow instance is a cross-log view, ordered by
  ts under the single-driver invariant).
end note

== Conversation start ==
User -> Host : engage a facilitator agent (VMO / RTE / SM)\nwith a request — a question or an intent
Host -> Harness : hook ""sessionStart"" (agent session)
alt C7 gate — agent + host session ids resolve to a framework agent
  Harness -> Harness : ""0 register-session"" — FIRST at every framework session:\nregisters sessionId (no parent here) + creates the session log
  Harness -> Harness : no open dispatch — an orchestrator session:\n""1 resolve-workflow-instructions"" — selection + return-handling instructions\n(the selection instruction references the facilitated workflows)\n""2 resolve-workflow-skills"" — selection + procedure skills
  Harness --> Host : context to inject
  Host --> Orch : session opens carrying the workflow instructions:\nthe ""*-handling"" reaction for every selection and harness return
else foreign session
  Harness --> Host : pass through — untouched, unlogged
end

== Workflow selection (no harness call) ==
Orch -> Orch : per ""workflow-selection-handling"" instruction —\nmatch the user's intent to one facilitated workflow
alt the intent maps to one workflow (the orchestrator's selection skill)
  Orch --> User : proposes it
else ambiguous or unmatched intent (optional engagement turns)
  Orch --> User : engages — answers, asks which workflow to enter
  User -> Orch : clarifies the intent
end
User -> Orch : assent — start the workflow\n(or continue an unfinished one — the harness\nresumes its latest open instance)

loop until ""3 resolve-step"" resolves no-next-step

== Step resolution ==
Orch -> Harness : adapter-mediated invocation:\n""3 resolve-step"" (workflowSlug)
Harness -> Harness : deduce the instance — continue the latest open one,\nor mint a new instance id (the opening is this very\nlog entry — no dedicated file, no id returned)
Harness --> Orch : step resolution — the configured step, verbatim
Orch -> Harness : adapter-mediated invocation:\n""4 resolve-step-model"" (session attribution only — standalone call)
Harness -> Harness : deduce the session's in-flight step;\ncapabilities × catalog → model profile
Harness --> Orch : model profile (the adapter maps it\nto the host model id)
Orch -> Orch : per ""step-resolution-handling"" instruction —\nrelay the resolution + profile verbatim

== Step dispatch (1 step = 1 agent = 1 session = 1 artifact) ==
Orch -> Host : ""runSubagent"" (the resolution verbatim:\nactor, model profile, skills, instructions)
Host -> Harness : hook ""preToolUse"" dispatch (step-open)
Harness -> Harness : ""5 check-step-preconditions"" — THE enforcement point\n(journals to the dispatching facilitator session's log)
alt preconditions hold
  Harness --> Host : allow
else a precondition fails
  Harness --> Host : deny + reports
  Host --> Orch : dispatch blocked, reports returned
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — produce the missing\nstate (via a prior step or the user), dispatch again
end
Host -> Harness : hook ""sessionStart"" (step session)
Harness -> Harness : ""0 register-session"" — registers the step session:\nsessionId + parentSessionId (the dispatching session)
Harness -> Harness : unresolved step-resolution correlated (exact match via parentSessionId,\nresolution-actor heuristic as fallback) — a step session:\n""6 resolve-step-instructions"" — the step's refs\n""7 resolve-step-skills"" — the step's skills
Harness --> Host : context to inject
Host --> Sub : session carries the step's constraints

== Step work — every write guarded ==
Sub -> Host : write artifact (host write tool)
Host -> Harness : hook ""preToolUse"" write (write-open)
Harness -> Harness : ""8 check-step-authorization""
alt privilege granted
  Harness --> Host : allow (staging baseline clean against HEAD)
  Host -> Host : execute the write — lands in the working tree\n(the staging area, not yet workspace state)
else no grant
  Harness --> Host : deny (missing privilege)
  Host --> Sub : write blocked, report returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — proceed without the write,\nor return it to the orchestrator (privileged-author route)
end
Host -> Harness : hook ""postToolUse"" write (write-close)
Harness -> Harness : ""9 check-step-artifact"" — the commit gate:\nvalidate the staged bytes
alt write is schema-valid
  Harness -> Harness : commit the staged write — workspace state\n(HEAD) advances atomically, attributed to the session
  Harness --> Host : outcome ""valid""
else invalid write
  Harness -> Harness : discard the staged write — restore from HEAD /\ndelete new: committed state never held the invalid\nbytes (C6 — transactional by construction)
  Harness --> Host : outcome ""reverted"" + failure message
  Host --> Sub : failure message returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — rewrite per the\nfailure message and retry the write
end

== Step close ==
Sub --> Host : step session ends
Host -> Harness : hook ""postToolUse"" dispatch (step-close)
Harness -> Harness : ""10 check-step-postconditions"" — THE evaluation point:\nthe step outcome logs against the state the step left\n(journals to the dispatching facilitator session's log)
alt postconditions hold — step journaled executed
  Harness --> Host : outcome pass
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns — next iteration resolves the next step
else postconditions fail — step not journaled executed
  Harness --> Host : outcome fail + reports
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns with reports
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — retry inside the workflow,\ninvisible to the user: the next iteration re-resolves the failed step\n(the harness governs the sequencing, not the agent)
end

end

== Workflow return ==
Orch -> Harness : adapter-mediated invocation:\n""3 resolve-step"" (workflowSlug)
Harness --> Orch : ""no-next-step""\n(a reversible observation — never "done")
Orch -> Orch : per ""no-next-step-handling"" instruction\n(it names the advisory successors)
Orch --> User : end-to-end workflow results (delivered artifacts)\n+ options: reiterate the workflow / take a successor
note right of Orch
  The user sees workflow results only —
  never intermediate step results.
  Step retries happen inside the workflow:
  re-resolution on negative reports (invariant 7).
end note

== Conversation close ==
Host -> Harness : hook ""stop"" / ""sessionEnd""
Harness -> Harness : adapter telemetry only — not a boundary:\nno function runs, nothing journals

== Global checks (direct session invocation — human terminal / CI system session) ==
User -> Harness : bash wrapper (human) or CI step (system):\n""0 register-session"" — wrapper-minted sessionId\nor the CI platform's ambient run id
User -> Harness : ""11 check-workspace""
Harness --> User : workspace checks (C6 proven when empty)
User -> Harness : ""12 check-configuration""
Harness --> User : configuration checks (.env layout, conf files, adapters)
note right of Harness
  CI pipelines run 11 on the workspace
  repository and 12 on the framework
  repository as merge gates — journaled
  to the invoking session's log like any
  other function.
end note

@enduml
